WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.182 --> 00:00:15.603
and Mikhail rode down the streets of St.

2
00:00:15.664 --> 00:00:22.787
Petersburg. The buildings were grand but old, and birds had built nests in the stone cracks.

3
00:00:24.068 --> 00:00:26.509
Vinnie saw that many people were poor.

4
00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.932
Children with sad, hungry eyes were in the streets.

5
00:00:32.348 --> 00:00:36.752
The old people sitting in front of the buildings looked tired and sick.

6
00:00:38.153 --> 00:00:42.156
"People don't look very happy," Vinnie said to Mikhail.

7
00:00:43.517 --> 00:00:45.058
Mikhail nodded sadly.

8
00:00:45.078 --> 00:00:49.181
"Many people are angry at the royal family.

9
00:00:50.282 --> 00:00:53.104
The czar does not know how people really live."

10
00:00:53.124 --> 00:00:57.167
"Mikhail," his father said, sharply.

11
00:00:57.187 --> 00:00:58.328
"Keep silent."

12
00:00:59.948 --> 00:01:03.471
"But, Papa, even you said that change must happen!"

13
00:01:04.091 --> 00:01:05.092
Mikhail cried.

14
00:01:05.112 --> 00:01:11.216
"We do not speak of these matters in the street," Mikhail's father said nervously.

15
00:01:11.236 --> 00:01:14.279
"The czar's spies are everywhere."

16
00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:18.462
Inside the palace, Mandy was in trouble.

17
00:01:19.803 --> 00:01:22.845
The ruffle of Anna's dress was muddy and stained.

18
00:01:22.865 --> 00:01:25.507
"Clean this up now!"

19
00:01:26.087 --> 00:01:26.788
said Anna.

20
00:01:28.316 --> 00:01:32.037
She pulled the ruffle off her dress and handed it to Mandy.

21
00:01:33.718 --> 00:01:37.259
Then a servant led the ballerina down a hallway.

22
00:01:38.919 --> 00:01:43.080
As she walked off, Anna's dress looked shorter and very plain.

23
00:01:44.621 --> 00:01:48.802
Another servant motioned to Mandy: "Come to the kitchen!

24
00:01:49.262 --> 00:01:50.343
We'll clean it there."

25
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:55.184
In the halls and rooms of the palace, everything shone.

26
00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:59.221
It was as if gold had been poured on the walls.

27
00:02:00.441 --> 00:02:04.022
The furniture was covered in thick purple and red velvet.

28
00:02:05.302 --> 00:02:06.963
Crystal lights sparkled.

29
00:02:06.983 --> 00:02:11.324
"First time in the Winter Palace?"

30
00:02:11.984 --> 00:02:12.804
asked the servant.

31
00:02:12.824 --> 00:02:18.546
"Yes, it's beautiful," Mandy exclaimed.

32
00:02:18.566 --> 00:02:22.727
"The royal family is usually here only in winter.

33
00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:27.733
But this year, the Romanovs are staying longer," explained the servant.

34
00:02:27.753 --> 00:02:34.259
"Romanov that name sounds familiar," Mandy thought.

35
00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.544
Outside the kitchen, they passed delivery men carrying baskets of flowers.

36
00:02:42.245 --> 00:02:45.788
A little while earlier, Vinnie had arrived at the palace.

37
00:02:47.149 --> 00:02:51.773
In the square outside, he unloaded baskets of flowers from a wagon.

38
00:02:51.793 --> 00:02:56.593
"Wow! Look at how big the palace is!"

39
00:02:57.113 --> 00:02:58.333
he cried, staring.

40
00:02:58.353 --> 00:03:03.056
"Come, we have work to do," said Mikhail's father.

41
00:03:04.776 --> 00:03:10.139
Inside, Vinnie passed a servant and a little girl carrying some wrinkled fabric.

42
00:03:11.559 --> 00:03:16.802
The tall basket of flowers blocked his vision, and he didn't see that it was Mandy.

43
00:03:18.503 --> 00:03:21.224
Mandy cleaned the ruffle as best as she could.

44
00:03:22.812 --> 00:03:26.174
Then she left the kitchen to take it to Miss Pavlova.

45
00:03:27.555 --> 00:03:31.017
She paused in a hall to look at a royal family portrait.

46
00:03:32.477 --> 00:03:37.400
In the painting, there were five children—four girls and a young boy.

47
00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:44.544
"Romanov Mandy said aloud, looking more closely at the picture.

48
00:03:44.564 --> 00:03:47.125
"Awful, isn't it?"

49
00:03:47.626 --> 00:03:51.488
said a girl a bit older than Mandy who was standing nearby.

50
00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.383
She wore a pink dress with matching ribbons in her hair.

51
00:03:56.403 --> 00:04:02.188
"I think it's a fine picture," Mandy said nervously.

52
00:04:02.208 --> 00:04:07.533
"It doesn't look like me at all," the girl complained playfully.

53
00:04:08.834 --> 00:04:10.815
Mandy looked at the picture again.

54
00:04:12.277 --> 00:04:15.719
This girl must be the one sitting to the right of the boy.

55
00:04:15.739 --> 00:04:20.764
"You do look better in real life," admitted Mandy.

56
00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.209
The girl looked curiously at Mandy.

57
00:04:25.729 --> 00:04:27.850
Then she said, "I like you.

58
00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:29.571
You're very honest."

59
00:04:31.231 --> 00:04:32.132
Mandy smiled.

60
00:04:32.152 --> 00:04:33.752
"I'm Mandy.

61
00:04:34.232 --> 00:04:36.053
I need to find Miss Pavlova.

62
00:04:36.553 --> 00:04:37.934
Do you know where she is?"

63
00:04:37.954 --> 00:04:42.855
"Yes. She is with my parents," replied the girl.

64
00:04:42.875 --> 00:04:44.976
"My name is Anastasia."
